### P0.7 Placement guardrails (reject weak two-phone layouts)

**File:** `Lib/Tracking.py` or new `Lib/CalibrationQuality.py` called from `_observe_calibration` / post-calibration

**Required change:**
- After extrinsics estimated (automatic mode), compute approximate angle between camera forward vectors in room space; if **< 30°** (phones nearly co-linear), set `calibration_hint = "Phones see the same angle; move one phone ~90° to the side"` and do not set `_session_calibrated = True`.
- If triangulation baseline (distance between camera centers) < 0.5 m in normalized solve, same failure mode.

**Tests:** synthetic two-camera fixtures in `tests/test_tracking.py` with parallel vs orthogonal setups.

